-- title:
--   Theorem 3.6 — the $4L/(k(k+1))$ rate of the accelerated gradient method (corrected)
-- statement:
--   Let $X$ be closed convex in a normed space, $\nu$ a distance generating function on $X$ with prox-function $V$, and $f$ convex and differentiable along $X$ with $L$-Lipschitz gradient $\nabla f$. Run the accelerated gradient method (3.3.4)–(3.3.6) with $\mu=0$ from $x_0=\bar x_0\in X$ and the schedule $q_t=\alpha_t=\tfrac2{t+1}$, $\gamma_t=\tfrac t{2L}$. Then for every $k\ge 1$,
--   $$f(\bar x_k)-f(x^*)\le\frac{4L}{k(k+1)}V(x_0,x^*).$$
--
--   **Formalization Note.** The retired statement had no convexity hypothesis on $f$ at all and a free $V$ (so $V\equiv 0$ made the bound $0$; disproved). The retired version took $V$ as a free function (with at most nonnegativity and a three-point identity), which admits $V\equiv 0$; the corrected version uses `FirstOrderOpt.Prox.DistanceGeneratingFunction.V`, the prox-function of a distance generating function on $X$ exactly as in §3.2. The gradient $\nabla f$ is tied to $f$ (`HasFDerivWithinAt` along $X$) with the Lipschitz condition (3.3.2) stated on $\nabla f$ itself, as in the book. Convexity of $f$ is stated through the gradient inequality on $X$.
-- source:
--   Lan, First-order and Stochastic Optimization Methods for Machine Learning, Springer 2020, p. 66, Theorem 3.6 ("in particular")

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_FirstOrderOpt_Prox_DistanceGeneratingFunction

namespace FirstOrderOpt.Deterministic

open FirstOrderOpt.Prox

/-- Theorem 3.6, "in particular" instantiation (the `4L/(k(k+1))` rate), Lan p. 66. Let `X` be
closed convex, `ν` a distance generating function on `X` with prox-function `V = ν.V`, and `f`
convex and differentiable along `X` with `L`-Lipschitz gradient `fGrad` (3.3.2). Let
`(x t, xTilde t, xBar t)` be generated by the accelerated gradient method (3.3.4)–(3.3.6) with
`μ = 0`, `x 0 = xBar 0 ∈ X`, and the schedule `q t = α t = 2/(t+1)`, `γ t = t/(2L)`. Then for
every `k ≥ 1`, `f(xBar k) - f(x*) ≤ 4L/(k(k+1)) · V(x 0, x*)`.

Corrected version: `V` is the Bregman distance of a distance generating function (the retired
free `V` admitted `V ≡ 0`, making the bound `0`), `f` is convex with `fGrad` its `L`-Lipschitz
gradient (the retired statement had no convexity hypothesis at all), `X` is closed convex and
`x 0 = xBar 0`. -/
theorem accelerated_gradient_rate_v2 {E : Type*} [NormedAddCommGroup E] [NormedSpace ℝ E]
    (X : Set E) (hXconv : Convex ℝ X) (hXclosed : IsClosed X)
    (ν : DistanceGeneratingFunction X)
    (f : E → ℝ) (L : ℝ) (hL : 0 < L)
    (fGrad : E → E →L[ℝ] ℝ)
    (hGrad : ∀ x ∈ X, HasFDerivWithinAt f (fGrad x) X x)
    (hSmooth : ∀ x ∈ X, ∀ y ∈ X, ‖fGrad x - fGrad y‖ ≤ L * ‖x - y‖)
    (hConvex : ∀ x ∈ X, ∀ y ∈ X, f x + (fGrad x) (y - x) ≤ f y)
    (x xTilde xBar : ℕ → E)
    (hx : ∀ t, x t ∈ X) (hxBar0 : xBar 0 = x 0)
    (k : ℕ) (hk : 1 ≤ k)
    (hTildeDef : ∀ t : ℕ, 1 ≤ t → t ≤ k →
      xTilde t = (1 - 2 / ((t : ℝ) + 1)) • xBar (t - 1) + (2 / ((t : ℝ) + 1)) • x (t - 1))
    (hxDef : ∀ t : ℕ, 1 ≤ t → t ≤ k → ∀ y ∈ X,
      ((t : ℝ) / (2 * L)) * (fGrad (xTilde t)) (x t) + ν.V (x (t - 1)) (x t) ≤
        ((t : ℝ) / (2 * L)) * (fGrad (xTilde t)) y + ν.V (x (t - 1)) y)
    (hBarDef : ∀ t : ℕ, 1 ≤ t → t ≤ k →
      xBar t = (1 - 2 / ((t : ℝ) + 1)) • xBar (t - 1) + (2 / ((t : ℝ) + 1)) • x t)
    (xstar : E) (hxstar : xstar ∈ X) (hxstar_opt : ∀ y ∈ X, f xstar ≤ f y) :
    f (xBar k) - f xstar ≤ (4 * L) / ((k : ℝ) * ((k : ℝ) + 1)) * ν.V (x 0) xstar := by sorry

end FirstOrderOpt.Deterministic
